    </div>

    <div class="disclaimer">
      This is not financial advice. Every argument here is the author's reading of public documents. Neither source mentions XRP, Ripple, or the XRP Ledger; all connections drawn are interpretive. Sources: Shin, H.S., "Tokenomics and blockchain fragmentation," BIS Working Papers no 1335, March 2026 (bis.org/publ/work1335.pdf); Eidan, Frost, Kansal, Lewrick, Lim and Rybarczyk, "Blockchain consensus mechanisms and fragmentation," BIS Bulletin no 126, 6 July 2026 (bis.org/publ/bisbull126.pdf). XRPL consensus and fee mechanics from xrpl.org documentation; the ~35 default-UNL validator count is approximate. Ronin bridge loss figure as cited in the Bulletin. Do your own research.
